      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santee%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Santee serves as the principal village of the Santee Sioux Reservation in Knox County, Nebraska.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santee%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Santee Sioux were originally part of the Great Sioux Nation whose lands stretched from eastern Minnesota to the Big Horn Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://nativepartnership.org/nebraska-santee-sioux/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Santee division of the Sioux Nation consists of four bands: Mdewakantonwan, Wahpeton, Sisseton, and Wahpekute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://santeesiouxnation.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Santee Sioux were initially moved to a site on the Missouri River about 100 miles from Fort Randall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://nativepartnership.org/nebraska-santee-sioux/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Santee Tribe were woodlands people living in semi‑permanent villages and practicing some farming.",
